      "title": "Z-Image anchor method and limits",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Z-Image Turbo identity anchor I2I\n\nThis is an experimental community anchor technique, not a native identity-edit model. It places the identity portrait on both sides of the target, protects those anchors with a latent noise mask, and regenerates only the center. Expect roughly three times the pixels and slower sampling. Start at denoise 0.82; try 0.70-0.90. Compare the native crop and identity score honestly—do not treat a later ReActor pass as Z-Image identity performance.\n\nSources: Tongyi-MAI Z-Image Turbo, jayn7 Q8 GGUF, and the highly upvoted community Anchor Workflow Z-Image Turbo."
      ]
    }
